{"selected": "title-29-ch4B", "prepared_chars": 99071, "focus": [0, 23969], "first_opportunity": {"window_index": 0, "occurrence_id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:reference:29da084597028e85f67db773a33127d3a88d56dc6e04ccd333984e58da0874ec", "source_unit": "/us/usc/t29/s49a", "href": "/us/usc/t29/s49c", "quote": "section 49c of this title", "target_id": "urn:rulespec:document-understanding:reference-target:2d7745217e256fc32f25f11be218c941d2f6e0f6eb815e25d19d7936cb4e750b", "target_start": 27585, "target_end": 29982, "target_preview": "§ 49c. Acceptance by States; creation of State agencies\n\nIn order to obtain the benefits of appropriations apportioned under section 49d of this title, a State shall, pursuant to State statute, accept the provisions of this chapter and, in accordance with such State statute, the Governor shall designate or authorize the creation of a State agency vested with all powers necessary to cooperate with the Secretary under this chapter.\n\n(June 6, 1933, ch. 49, § 4, 48 Stat. 114; Pub. L. 105–220, title III, § 303, Aug. 7, 1998, 112 Stat. 1081.)\n\nEditorial Notes\n\nAmendments\n\n1998—Pub. L. 105–220 substituted “, pursuant to State statute,” for “, throug"}}
